        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.267,
            0.744,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fossil fuels are found in limited quantities. Hence, we will soon run out of fossil fuels if we continue to use them in the manner that we currently do. To avoid such a situation, we need to explore alternate sources of energy. When fossil fuels are burnt, smoke and carbon dioxide gas are produced which pollutes the air. Over-dependence on fossil fuels for transportation and as domestic fuels has resulted in large scale air pollution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.452,
            0.599,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us do our bit to conserve the fossil fuels by—"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.476,
            0.536,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Walking or cycling to nearby places."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.5,
            0.406,
            0.521
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Using public transport."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.525,
            0.386,
            0.545
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suggest some more ways."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.577,
            0.639,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11.7 Natural Resources: renewable and non-renewable"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.638,
            0.743,
            0.843
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Nature’s treasures fulfill our needs. They are essential resources to sustain all life forms on the Earth. For example, we get heat and light from the Sun, water from rivers, and food from plants and animals. These resources which we get from nature are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "natural resources.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We also use natural resources to make many useful things for our convenience. For example, electric bulbs, furniture, solar panels, bicycles, etc., make our lives comfortable. All such resources created by human beings are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "human-made resources.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.843,
            0.743,
            0.906
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have learnt about various natural resources, such as air, water, energy from the Sun, forests, soil, rocks, minerals and fossil fuels. Some of these natural resources"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.891,
            0.764,
            0.908,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Nature’s Treasures"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
